]}, "highlightText": "", "language": "english", "persons": [], "text": "The Senate Commerce Committee will hold a hearing about safeguarding consumers' data privacy (https://www.commerce.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/pressreleases?ID=240B5C17-CBD5-4039-A9E4-CF2FADFF4712) on Sept. 26, the panel announced. Witnesses include Keith Enright, the chief privacy officer of Alphabet Inc.'s (GOOGL)(GOOGL) Google and Andrew DeVore, vice president and associate general counsel of Amazon (AMZN). Executives from AT&T (T), Twitter (TWTR), Apple (AAPL) and Charter Communications (CHTR) will also testify, the committee said.\n-Robert Schroeder;\n 0946ET\n ", "external_links": ["https://www.commerce.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/pressreleases?ID=240B5C17-CBD5-4039-A9E4-CF2FADFF4712)", "http://www.addthis.com/bookmark.php?v=250"], "published": "2018-09-12T03:00:00.000+03:00", "crawled": "2018-09-12T17:54:02.049+03:00", "highlightTitle": ""}